# proposed-styles-patch.diff
#
# NOT APPLIED. @blakeui/styles is not edited without Greg's explicit sign-off,
# so every fix that lands in that package is written here instead.
#
# Contents
# --------
#  1. Build assertion (audit §1). The published tarballs are NOT broken — all
#     nine versions of @blakeui/styles and @blakeui/react resolve every relative
#     @import cleanly, verified by extracting each tarball and by compiling
#     @blakeui/react@1.3.0's CSS entry end-to-end with the Tailwind CLI. No
#     copy fix is needed. What is missing is the guard: the docs site resolves
#     @blakeui/styles through the workspace symlink to the SOURCE tree, so a
#     dist that is missing component stylesheets would ship green. The new
#     scripts/assert-css-imports.mjs runs inside the normal build, after the CSS
#     copy step and before minification, and exits non-zero listing every
#     unresolved relative @import.
#
#     Verified: temporarily skipping the copy of components/tabs.css made the
#     build fail with
#         ❌ 1 unresolved relative @import in dist:
#            dist/components/index.css  →  ./tabs.css
#     and a non-zero exit; restoring the copy made it pass again.
#
#  2. CSS defect (a) — `:focus-visible:not(:focus)` is unsatisfiable. A
#     :focus-visible element always also matches :focus, so the :not(:focus)
#     arm can never hold and the package focus ring was painted only when the
#     JavaScript layer set data-focus-visible. 38 occurrences across 27
#     component stylesheets. popover.css already carried the corrected form
#     plus a comment explaining why, and is untouched; this applies the same
#     correction everywhere else.
#
#     Verified in Chrome against a compiled bundle: with the old selector a
#     keyboard-focused `.button` reported --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000 (no ring);
#     with the fix it reports 0 0 0 calc(2px + 2px) oklch(...) and the ring
#     renders.
#
#  3. CSS defect (b) — `:focus-visible` on a root that React Aria renders as a
#     <label>. Checkbox, Switch and Radio each render `<label>` wrapping a
#     visually hidden `<input>`. Focus lands on the input, and :focus-visible
#     matches the focused element only — it does not propagate to ancestors —
#     so `.checkbox:focus-visible`, `.switch:focus-visible` and
#     `.radio:focus-visible` can never match. Replaced with
#     `:has(:focus-visible)`, which reaches up from the focused input.
#
#     Verified in Chrome: with the input keyboard-focused,
#     root.matches(':focus-visible') === false while
#     root.matches(':has(:focus-visible)') === true, and the control's ring
#     renders with no JavaScript involved.
#
# Apply with:
#     git apply proposed-styles-patch.diff
#
